<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexei Kulabukhov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1919</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexei Kulabukhov was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> priest and member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuban-rada">Kuban Rada</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a>, a supporter of Kuban autonomy and closer ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. In 1919 he was among the Kuban delegates in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> who signed a treaty of friendship with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mountainous-republic-of-the-northern-caucasus">Mountainous Republic of the Northern Caucasus</a>, and on Denikin's orders he was court-martialled and hanged at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Yekaterinodar</a> in November 1919.</p></div>
